# Release staging and output directories. The CI lanes that wrote to
# `staging/` and uploaded from `release/` were retired on 2026-11-04, so
# nothing writes them any more; they stay ignored because the release
# scripts can still produce them locally, and the published artifacts live
# on GitHub Releases, not in git.
#
# `dist/` joins them for the same reason: the release tooling writes its
# archives there at the repository root. MEDIDO 2026-10-22, on this machine
# `dist/` was only ignored by the operator's global gitignore, so the
# property lived in ~/.config/git/ignore and not in the repository: on any
# other machine the tarballs showed up as untracked, one `git add -A` away
# from being committed.
/staging/
/release/
/dist/

