# Whole `docs/` directory is LOCAL ONLY per user decision (2026-06-24).
# The directory remains on disk for developer reference (ADRs, plans,
# roadmaps, screenshots, etc.) but is not part of the git-tracked
# source. Pre-existing ADR files remain in git history (commits before
# this .gitignore entry was added) — only future commits are affected.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-10-01: this rule read `docs/`, excluding the DIRECTORY.
# Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so every `!/docs/...`
# negation below it was inert. `docs/*` excludes the same paths but leaves
# `docs/` itself traversable, so negations work.
# Verified not to widen the policy: see
# crates/cognicode-cli/tests/gitignore_negation_contract.rs.
#
# NOTE: The ADRs in docs/adr/ are first-class documentation that the
# project relies on. There is deliberately no `!/docs/adr/` negation;
# ADRs are added with `git add -f docs/adr/ADR-NNN-...` and the ones
# already tracked predate this rule. That is the declared policy, and
# the contract test holds it rather than changing it.
docs/*

