# Root AGENTS.md is the tracked entrypoint. Per-developer notes remain
# untracked in AGENTS.local.md / CONTEXT.md.
docs/adr/
CONTEXT.md

# Production-ready action plan package (Post-PRF stabilization program,
# baseline `2991e5e2`). Tracked because it is the active roadmap
# addendum governing CR-* and ST-* work units. See ROADMAP-ADDENDUM.md.
# `!/docs/roadmap/` is required: without it, `docs/roadmap` stays excluded, git
# never descends into it, and the negations below match nothing. It is re-closed
# right after with `docs/roadmap/*`, so the exemption covers the addendum package
# and not the whole directory, which would otherwise pull in ephemeral files such
# as docs/roadmap/INSTALL.md.
!/docs/roadmap/
docs/roadmap/*
!/docs/roadmap/production-ready/
!/docs/roadmap/production-ready/**/
!/docs/roadmap/consumer-contracts/
!/docs/roadmap/consumer-contracts/**/

# NOTE: docs/debts/ is deliberately NOT exempted. It looks like it should be —
# `advisory_ignore_backing_contract` reads DEBT-SEC-001 in CI, so the register
# has to be tracked. But exempting the directory also exposes DEBT-SDDK-002..006,
# which exist on disk, were never committed, and all carry the line "local only,
# NEVER pushed to remote (ephemeral per AGENTS.md)". Making them trackable by
# default is a policy decision about the local-only rule of 2026-06-24, not a
# side effect of fixing the negations.
#
# The rule that settled it: a debt register is tracked if and only if a gate
# reads it, and a file declaring itself local-only is never tracked. DEBT-SEC-001
# is the single exception because the advisories gate depends on it, and that
# exception is recorded rather than smuggled in. DEBT-SDDK-006 was force-added
# alongside it while carrying the local-only header, which made it the only
# register contradicting itself; it has been untracked to match its siblings.
# `gitignore_negation_contract.rs` holds both directions of this rule.


# LadybugDB runtime artifacts
cognicode.lbug
cognicode.lbug.wal

# An UAT report from the retired UAT class. The class is gone; the file is
# still ignored so a leftover from a past run does not become an untracked
# file that somebody commits.
uat-guided-v1.0.0-current.html

# `crates/cognicode-cli/src/bin/` holds SOURCE, not build output: the package
# produces several binaries (`cogh`, `cognicode`, `cognicode-release`).
# A very common global ignore pattern is a bare `bin/`, which silently drops NEW
# files added there while leaving already-tracked ones alone. That is exactly how
# `src/bin/release.rs` was lost on the first v0.95.0 release attempt: local builds
# passed and CI failed with "can't find bin". A repository-level negation wins
# over core.excludesFile, so declare the layout here.
!crates/cognicode-cli/src/bin/
sandbox/scripts/tests/__pycache__/
*.cdx.json
*.cdx.xml

# Compat matrix binaries (Post-PRF L1.3): binarios legacy para tests
# de compat (extraídos de releases publicados, no commiteados).
sandbox/.compat/

# Python bytecode caches. Running the Python contract suite locally produces
# these. Without the ignore they show up as untracked noise on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Mutation reports. `cargo mutants` writes its outcome — caught, missed,
# timeout — into `mutants.out/`, and renames the previous run to
# `mutants.out.old/`. The report is the evidence of the gate step, but it is
# a local artefact: the receipt in the JOURNAL is what gets committed.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# SDDK orchestration scratch. `sddk` writes these into the working directory
# when a command is run from the repo root; they are session output, never
# project state. The unit's real evidence lives under docs/, not here.
.sddk-scratch/
out-*.json

# PipelineK run databases. The lanes that wrote one per repository are gone
# as of 2026-11-04; the ignore stays so a local `pipelinek run` leaves no
# untracked noise.
.pipelinek/

# PipelineK control-root state. When `--control-root` points at the repository
# instead of `.pipelinek`, the runtime writes its leases, output-plane streams
# and last-run pointers into the working tree. Measured 2026-10-15: 32 such
# files were tracked and would have shipped in a release tarball. They are
# per-run scratch, not product, and two of them are `*.lock` files whose whole
# purpose is to disappear with the process that held them.
/leases/
/last-run/
/output-plane/
/retry-control/
/wait-until-control/
# PipelineK durable-shell per-step scratch directories: UUID-prefixed
# runtime artifacts. They appear at the repo root and the run id cannot
# be listed by name, so the pattern is a UUID match.

# PipelineK durable-shell steps written at the repository root. MEDIDO
# 2026-10-15: un run cuyo `--control-root` resuelve a `<cwd>` deja un
# directorio por step, con nombre `<run-uuid>-s<indice>-<step>/`, que
# contiene `script.sh`, `result.txt` y `wrapper.sh`. Son scratch de una
# ejecucion, no producto, y aparecen como untracked en cada `git status`.
# El mismo contrato que vigila `leases/` y `last-run/` los vigila ahora.
/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*[0-9a-f]*-[0-9a-z]*-s[0-9]*-[0-9]*/
.goal-compass/

# Backlog.md: la bandeja de trabajo local. Los ficheros de planificación no se
# rastrean en Git (política de documentos privados): son estado del agente, no
# fuente del producto. Lo que se deriva de ellos —identificadores de tarea y
# su recibo— se anota en el Journal, que sí es la autoridad versionada.
.backlog/

# La proyección privada de la agenda (roadmap, SPEC, ADR y el paquete de
# especificaciones) sigue la misma política: son estado del agente, no fuente
# del producto. Lo que se deriva de ellos —identificadores de tarea y su
# recibo— se anota en el Journal, que sí es la autoridad versionada.
planning/

.codegraph/

